<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vladimir Lenin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1870">1870</a>–<a href="/years/1924">1924</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Vladimir Ilyich Ulyanov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vladimir Lenin was a Russian revolutionary who led the Bolshevik party. He organised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a> of 1917, headed the government of Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> through the Civil War and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1922. His New Economic Policy of 1921 allowed limited private trade. After strokes from 1922 he died in 1924, and his ideas, as Leninism, shaped later communist states.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vladimir-lenin.jpg" alt="Vladimir Lenin" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, presumably official · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lenin_in_1920_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
